sentences.text:
12. Accordingly, the petitioner, Shri Abani Mudoi @ Aboni, shall be released on regular bail, in connection with Garamur P.S. Case No. 42/2025 registered under Sections 123/274/275 of BNS,
2023 (corresponding to G.R. No. 82/2025), on furnishing a bail bond of Rs.15,000/- (Rupees Fifteen Thousand) only, along with 2 (two) local sureties each of the like amount to the satisfaction of the learned Chief Judicial Magistrate, Majuli, subject to the following conditions;
(1) The accused petitioner, herein, shall co-operate with the Investigating Officer in the investigation of the case;
Page No.# 4/4 (2) The accused petitioner, herein, shall appear before the Investigating Officer as and when called for, for the purpose of investigation of the case;
(3) The accused petitioner, herein, shall not directly or indirectly make any inducement, threat or promise to any person(s), acquainted with the facts of the case so as to dissuade him/her from disclosing the same to the Investigating Officer;
(4) The accused petitioner, herein, shall not leave the jurisdiction of the learned Chief Judicial Magistrate, Majuli, without prior permission;
13.

